The playbook runs on the lab host itself. bootstrap.sh clones this repository
onto the host and runs site.yml against localhost over the local connection,
which is why the only committed inventory is localhost.yml, and why the vault
and its password live on the host under /etc/hcw/ansible and nowhere else.

Running from a workstation is not a supported path in this repository: the
vault file and its password are host-local, so a workstation run would need
copies of both, and this repository deliberately gives no instructions for
carrying a vault password off the host. To run the playbook, or to see what a
run would change, do it on the host. Bash, as the hcwadmin user the hardening
role created:

    sudo /opt/hcw-src/lab-host/bootstrap.sh

    sudo /opt/hcw-src/lab-host/bootstrap.sh --check --diff

lab-host/README.md is the full account of both commands and of what a
successful run prints.
